## QG-9 V2 protected theorem earned — support bound improves 5 -> 4

Exact scientific head: `58536ef2898bdd3f7a68e2bfde9b5aedef876a2e`.
Protected workflow: `orion-qg-qg9-support4` run `32490719629`; artifact `9449659633`, digest `sha256:fdcf4dbec8390f5408f6f5c721f5e2a7f43519eef563c3c7000ba2a47a0a86d2`.

Earned terminal:
`QG9_RANK2_ALL_N_SUPPORT4_SUFFICIENCY_MACHINE_CHECKED`

Machine facts:
- production algebra bound exactly;
- 28 local descriptors / 240 concrete representatives / 119,808 adversarial action-target cost cases;
- broad QG-1-irreducible support-5 boundary: **324 patterns**, all **324/324** admit a five-signature-preserving, support-reducing combined move with worst-case cost <=0 for every central choice;
- independent generic implementation reproduces 324/324 and zero unsafe;
- native ORION-Q: `ACCEPT_SUPPORT4`;
- canonical QG-1 supplies all-n support<=5, so closing every support-5 irreducible boundary gives all-n support<=4 by lexicographic descent.

Hostile boundary control:
- support-4 domain: **432** retained irreducible patterns;
- **36** remain unsafe under this deletion-only combined grammar.
- therefore `support3_authority=false` and `tightness_authority=false` remain mandatory.

Durable result/receipt commits now on PR #786 branch: `826fc872...` and `51d81c44...`.

Next research direction is a separately frozen richer support-nonincreasing **relabel + delete** edit grammar against those 36 support-4 survivors; V2 itself will not be mutated.

## QG-9 V3 protected theorem earned — support bound improves 4 -> 3

Exact scientific head after engineering-only tie-break repair: `66de4da5a6e029fac632575c3a97590cfc866092`.
Protected workflow: `orion-qg-qg9-support3` run `32492395951`; artifact `9450349107`, digest `sha256:f8757808d924ed3f1efa72c1c65efab944a35401cf7c8ec68d1a0b65f3f73a40`.

Earned terminal:
`QG9_RANK2_ALL_N_SUPPORT3_SUFFICIENCY_MACHINE_CHECKED`

Protected facts:
- 46 concrete action-profile types under the support-nonincreasing relabel+delete grammar;
- all 36 V2 support-4 survivor descriptors expand to 288 concrete profile cases;
- **288/288 safe, 0 unsafe** under full five-signature preservation and adversarial all-target/all-central cost bounds;
- independent generic implementation reproduces the exact 288/0 result;
- native ORION-Q: `ACCEPT_SUPPORT3`;
- parent V2 protected support<=4 theorem binds exactly.

Broad support-3 anti-overclaim control: 180 V2-survivor descriptors -> 612 profile cases, 591 safe / 21 unsafe. Therefore V3 explicitly grants `support2_authority=false` and `tightness_authority=false`.

Durable result/receipt commits: `601a5ba3...`, `4d70700b...`.
Failed predecessor run `32492089671` is retained as engineering-only (`None` vs tuple tie-break); no scientific terminal was reached there.

Successor finding (exploratory only): all 21 broad support-3 unsafe cases appear to violate the full R6I nonzero/distinct two-generator Tag-label acceptance condition. This is now being tested in a separate prospectively frozen V4; V3 itself is immutable.

## QG-9 V4 protected theorem earned — support bound improves 3 -> 2

Exact scientific head: `0689e42cde3c5dffaf7f25a440060a3abd6e2116`.
Protected workflow: `orion-qg-qg9-support2` run `32493415691`; artifact `9450792101`, digest `sha256:8731f0516f65a0266753afa6113ecc44fd1b2700655fd020e9c6093d92d434ab`.

Earned terminal:
`QG9_RANK2_ALL_N_SUPPORT2_SUFFICIENCY_MACHINE_CHECKED`

Key protected evidence:
- parent V3 boundary reconstructs exactly: 252 support-3 irreducibles, 180 V2 survivors, 612 V3 profile cases, 21 broad unsafe;
- full R6I acceptance leaves **300 accepted support-3 profile cases, all 300 safe, 0 unsafe**;
- every one of the 21 broad unsafe cases violates the exact nonzero/distinct two-generator Tag-label rule (`r1_label=0` or `r0_label==r1_label`);
- independent generic implementation reproduces all counts and zero accepted support-3 unsafe;
- native ORION-Q: `ACCEPT_SUPPORT2`.

Hostile support-2 control:
- 72 QG-1-irreducible / V2-survivor descriptors;
- 144 V3 action-profile cases;
- **72 fully accepted**, of which **36 safe / 36 unsafe** under the current relabel grammar.
Thus support-1/tightness authority remains false.

Durable result/receipt commits: `59821126...`, `a80dbd57...`.

Next lane changes methodology: exact n=2 target-level tightness. A support-cap-1 exact referee will be compared against unrestricted/cap-2 on inverse-designed instances derived prospectively from the 36 accepted method obstructions. A strict gap would prove support 2 is actually necessary; absence will not self-promote support<=1.
